 Installation

1. Clone or copy the project

Clone the repository or copy the project into a folder, for example "AideSOS".

2. Install dependencies

npm install

3. Configure ".env"

PORT=3000
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_password
DB_NAME=sos_platform

4. Start the server

node server.js

5. Open the application

http://localhost:3000

«The database and tables are created automatically if they do not already exist. Existing tables are never modified.»

---

 API — HTTP Methods

Method| Route| Description
GET| "/api/test"| Checks the server and database
GET| "/api/contacts/:userId"| Displays a user's emergency contacts
POST| "/api/contacts"| Adds an emergency contact
DELETE| "/api/contacts/:id"| Deletes a contact
GET| "/api/centers"| Emergency centers (type + distance filter)
GET| "/api/helpers"| Nearby helpers (demo)
POST| "/api/alerts"| Creates an SOS alert
GET| "/api/alerts"| Emergency history (ACTIVE / CANCELLED)
POST| "/api/alerts/:id/cancel"| Cancels an SOS
POST| "/api/ai/analyze"| Analyzes an emergency description using AI

Examples

Add an emergency contact — POST

{
  "user_id": 1,
  "nom": "Mom",
  "telephone": "0320000000",
  "relation": "Mother"
}

Create an SOS — POST

{
  "user_id": 1,
  "type": "MEDICAL",
  "description": "I feel unwell",
  "latitude": -18.8792,
  "longitude": 47.5079
}

Find emergency centers according to the emergency type — GET

/api/centers?lat=-18.8792&lng=47.5079&type=MEDICAL

